{
  "content": "<h1><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"ControlAccounts\">Control Accounts</span> &mdash; <span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Customers\">Customers</span></h1><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts Amount And Automatic By ControlAccount ControlAccounts Count Custom Customer Customers On To ToDate Total\">Customer control accounts automatically track and summarize the total amounts owed by all your customers.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts AccountsReceivable Balance ControlAccount ControlAccounts Count Custom Customer Date General_ledger On To ToDate\">Instead of having individual accounts receivable entries cluttering your general ledger, control accounts consolidate all customer balances into a single, manageable account.</p><details><summary><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Name\">Name</span></summary><div><div class=\"my-4\"><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 pointer-events-none text-sm w-max\"><div class=\"grid grid-cols-[1.25rem_auto_1.25rem] bg-neutral-200 gap-[1px]\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 border-t border-t-white\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 font-bold text-neutral-500 text-shadow px-4 py-2 border-t border-t-white\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Name\">Name</span></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 border-t border-t-white\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div></div></div></div><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts And ChartOfAccounts ControlAccount Count Is Name On Port Reports\">The name identifies this control account in your <em>chart of accounts</em> and financial reports.</p><h2 translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts And ControlAccount ControlAccounts Count On\">Understanding Control Accounts</h2><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts Automatic Balance ControlAccount ControlAccounts Count Custom Customer From FromDate General_ledger On To ToDate\">Control accounts are special <em>general ledger</em> accounts that automatically summarize all individual customer balances from your <em>subsidiary ledger</em>.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Action Automatic Balance BalanceSheet ControlAccount Count Custom Customer Date On Rate To ToDate Total Transaction Transactions Update\">When you record transactions for any customer, the system automatically updates the relevant control account, ensuring your <em>balance sheet</em> always shows accurate total receivables.</p><h2 translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts ControlAccount ControlAccounts Count On\">Naming Your Control Accounts</h2><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account ControlAccount Count Name On\">Choose descriptive names that clearly identify the purpose of each control account, such as:</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Custom Customer On Sales To ToDate\">• <strong>Trade Receivables</strong> - For regular customer sales</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Custom Customer Customers Deposit From FromDate On Payment Payments Received To ToDate\">• <strong>Customer Deposits</strong> - For prepayments received from customers</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts Count Custom Customer On To ToDate\">• <strong>International Receivables</strong> - For foreign customer accounts</p><h2 translate=\"true\" keywords=\"And\">Benefits and Best Practices</h2><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts And Automatic ControlAccount ControlAccounts Count Custom Customer Error General_ledger Manual On Reconciliation To ToDate\">Control accounts provide automatic reconciliation between your detailed customer records and general ledger, eliminating manual work and reducing errors.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts ControlAccount ControlAccounts Count Create Current Custom Customer Group Is On Overdue Payment Rate Rent To ToDate\">For better financial analysis, create separate control accounts for different customer groups (domestic vs. international) or payment terms (current vs. overdue).</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts ChartOfAccounts Count Custom Customer Is To ToDate\">This approach keeps your <em>chart of accounts</em> clean while maintaining complete customer detail in the subsidiary records.</p></div></details><details><summary><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Group\">Group</span></summary><div><div class=\"my-4\"><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 pointer-events-none text-sm w-max\"><div class=\"grid grid-cols-[1.25rem_auto_1.25rem] bg-neutral-200 gap-[1px]\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 border-t border-t-white\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 font-bold text-neutral-500 text-shadow px-4 py-2 border-t border-t-white\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Group\">Group</span></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 border-t border-t-white\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div></div></div></div><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Balance BalanceSheet ControlAccount Count Group HasWhere Is On Port Reports Select\">Select the <em>balance sheet</em> group where this control account will appear in your financial reports.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts AccountsReceivable Assets ControlAccount ControlAccounts Count Current Custom Customer Group On Rent To ToDate\">Customer control accounts typically belong under <strong>Assets</strong> in a group like <strong>Current Assets</strong> or <strong>Accounts Receivable</strong>.</p></div></details>",
  "key": "customer-control-accounts"
}
